      "original_text": "An important innovation of our approach is the so-called Validation Feedback Loop (VFL). The idea is to continuously evaluate the accuracy of the performance predictions related to the derived models. In order to determine the prediction accuracy of a model, it is necessary to have a baseline. We use measurements from the real system as reference, which are available in the form of monitoring data. By comparing simulation data of the models with the monitoring data, it can be assessed how well the models represent the actually observed system in its current state. In case of high deviations, it is possible to intervene."
