      "text": "It is challenging to manually recognize and re-use architectural knowledge (AK) within issue tracking systems because most issues do not discuss architectural problems and AK is represented as unstructured text.",
      "original_text": "However, similar to other sources of AK (e.g. developer communities [19, 20] or simply Google searching [23]), it is challenging to manually recognize and re-use AK within issue tracking systems. First, the majority of issues do not discuss architectural problems [3]; instead, they focus on detailed development problems (e.g. bug fixing or testing). Second, text in issues is not explicitly structured and classified; rather, AK is represented as unstructured text within an issue’s description, comments and attachments."
