      "original_text": "This study focuses on providing a set of actionable solutions to violations of loose coupling related microservice best practices. In particular, we investigate three major Architectural Design Decisions (ADD) related to microservice coupling: Persistent Data Storage of Services related to data sharing via shared data storage; Service Interconnections related to the effects of intermediate system components, such as API gateways, as well as of asynchronous integration; and Dependencies through Shared Services related to direct, transitive, and cyclic dependencies between individual microservices."
