      "text": "Information related to different lifecycle phases of industrial assets is scattered across multiple sources, leading to broken information flow, duplication, inconsistency, and missing data, which causes inefficiencies in accessing and using this information.",
      "original_text": "A major problem of industrial systems are information silos. The information related to different lifecycle phases of an asset (e.g, a device, a production cell) is scattered across multiple information sources. These information sources are often maintained by different internal and external organizations and are interfaced by various applications. This leads to a broken information flow across the lifecycle of the assets because these information sources do not properly exchange information; some information may be duplicated or inconsistent while some others may be missing. As a result, significant amounts of time are usually required to find the relevant information, to convert the information to a suitable format, to pass the information to different tools, etc."
    }
  ],
  "research_questions": [],
  "background_concepts": [
    {
      "name": "Digital Twin",
      "description": "An evolving digital profile of the historical and current behavior of an asset together with all of its properties, encompassing elements such as ordering details, engineering parameters, operational information, and maintenance information, used to provide access to lifecycle information of assets.",
      "original_text": "Digital twins can be seen as a promising solution for providing access to the lifecycle information of their assets. The underlying definition of the trend has evolved over time. Initially, a digital twin was considered to be a high fidelity mathematical model of a physical device that could simulate the device as closely as possible. This definition has been enriched over the time to be an evolving digital profile of the historical and current behavior of an asset together with all of its properties, where an asset is anything of value for an organization such as a physical device, a subsystem, a plant, or a software entity. The information fragments contained in a digital twin are use case specific and often originate from different lifecycle phases. Typically, it encompasses elements such as ordering details, engineering parameters, operational information, and maintenance information."
    },
    {
      "name": "OPC UA",
      "description": "An industrial communication protocol (IEC 62541) used for machine-to-machine communication and information modeling, enabling devices to expose operational parameters and methods in a standardized way.",
      "original_text": "The operational parameter information of each drive is maintained within the drive firmware itself and served via an OPC UA (IEC 62541) server; hence, the drive is labeled as an OPC UA-Enabled Drive."
    },
    {
      "name": "Model View Controller (MVC) pattern",
      "description": "A software architectural pattern used to manage models, views, and controllers for digital twin components and models, facilitating visualization, interaction, and data management.",
      "original_text": "Within the Model Kind plugin, we adopt the Model View Controller (MVC) pattern to manage each model that is to be included in a digital twin. The information content corresponds to the Model component of this pattern. Since each model is defined based on a specific standard or in a proprietary format, there is a dedicated View associated to each model to visualize its content in a suitable format. Each model is also associated with a Controller, which communicates with the respective view and also populates the model by interacting with Information Gateway (view and controller satisfy R7)."
    }
  ],
  "contributions": [
