      "description": "A phenomenon where the implemented architecture diverges from the intended architecture due to uncontrolled software evolution causing design rule violations.",
      "original_text": "Architecture erosion is a phenomenon that occurs when the implemented (concrete) architecture of a software system diverges from its intended (planned) architecture\u0000[20]. In fact, it is a side effect of a non-controlled software evolution process in which changes made in the source code lead to architecture design rules violations\u0000[12]."
