      "original_text": "At the software architecture level, exceptions and their control flow can be described using the IFTC model\u0000[14] (Fig.\u0000 01). It captures the essence behind the exception handling constructs of the mainstream object-oriented program languages\u0000[10], such as Java and C#. Each software component (callee) can receive service requests from other components (caller). The callee processes the request and sends back normal responses or exceptions."
