      "original_text": "Existing work has shown that machine learning (ML) techniques can be effectively used at run time for selecting self-adaptation patterns that can help maintain adequate QoS levels. However, this class of approach suffers from learning bias, which induces accuracy problems that might lead to sub-optimal (or even unfeasible) adaptations in some situations."
